  "articleBody": "Installing new countertops can elevate your kitchen, but a few common missteps can really mess things up. Here's how to dodge those bullets:\n\n1.  **Don't Rush Templating:** A big mistake is templating before your cabinets are perfectly installed and level. This is a recipe for a poor fit and can cause delays later on. Make sure those cabinets are solid!\n2.  **Clear Communication is Key:** Be super clear about your sink type (undermount vs. top-mount), how many faucet holes you need, and your cooktop dimensions. Miscommunication here leads to incorrect cutouts, and nobody wants that.\n3.  **Plan Those Seams:** For long countertop runs or big islands, you need to think about where seams will go. Improper placement can be a visual distraction or even create weak spots. Talk to your installer about optimal seam locations.\n4.  **Support Your Overhangs:** If you have large cantilevers or overhangs, make sure they're properly supported with corbels or brackets. Skipping this can lead to cracks or breakage, especially with heavy materials like stone.\n5.  **Seal Properly (If Needed):** If you're getting porous stone, don't skip the sealing! Also, make sure you're using compatible cleaners. Neglecting this can lead to staining or etching over time. Your fabricator should guide you on this.\n\nAvoiding these issues will ensure your countertop installation goes smoothly and looks fantastic. If you're ever in doubt, the team at HH Remodeling LLC can provide expert guidance and installation across the Denver area.",
